{"name":"Elk Horn","hex":"#e9e2d3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"elk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Elkei."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various large species of deer such as the red deer, moose or wapiti (see usage notes)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/elk"},{"term":"horn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard growth of keratin that protrudes from the top of the head of certain animals, usually paired.","Any similar real or imaginary growth or projection such as the elongated tusk of a narwhal, the eyestalk of a snail, the pointed growth on the nose of a rhinoceros, or the hornlike projection on the head of a demon or similar."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Of an animal, to assault with the horns.","To furnish with horns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elk","blocks":[{"text":"The elk or wapiti is the second largest species within the deer family, Cervidae, and one of the largest terrestrial mammals in its native range of North America and Central and East Asia. The word \"elk\" originally referred to the European variety of the moose, Alces alces, but was transferred to Cervus canadensis by North American colonists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Jasper.Wapiti-Hirsch.P1033401.jpg/330px-Jasper.Wapiti-Hirsch.P1033401.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elk","wikidata":"Q180404"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Jasper.Wapiti-Hirsch.P1033401.jpg/500px-Jasper.Wapiti-Hirsch.P1033401.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Jasper.Wapiti-Hirsch.P1033401.jpg/1280px-Jasper.Wapiti-Hirsch.P1033401.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten